The authoritative rules are in `AGENTS.md` at the repo root — follow it.

Non-negotiables when editing this codebase:

- **Deterministic core, LLM explains.** Findings come from deterministic checks
  (thresholds/math/decoded events), never from a model. Don't add model-judgement
  logic to the server.
- **Offline & read-only.** The server only parses local files. Never add network I/O,
  vehicle actuation, or parameter writes — that is the project's safety guarantee.
- **No unsupported assumptions.** Every threshold/enum/default/fact must be backed by an
  authoritative source (ArduPilot wiki/firmware, MAVLink, MCP spec), cited in a comment
  and in `docs/SOURCES.md`. Label our own cut-offs as design choices.
- **Keep docs in sync.** Adding/renaming a check or MCP tool requires updating
  `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` (and `docs/SOURCES.md` for new thresholds);
  `tests/test_docs_sync.py` enforces it.
- **Tests gate everything.** `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `mypy ardupilot_mcp`
  and `pytest` must pass.

Adding a check = one module in `ardupilot_mcp/checks/` (decorated `@register_check`,
listed in `checks/__init__._CHECK_MODULES`) + one test in `tests/checks/`. See AGENTS.md.
